.TH CALL-DUCKER 1 "August 2026" "CallDucker 0.1.1"
.SH NAME
call-ducker \- configure automatic game-audio adjustment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B call-ducker
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B CallDucker
opens the GNOME preferences window for the CallDucker user service. Closing
the window does not stop automatic volume adjustment. The service is disabled until the
user explicitly selects Enable CallDucker. During a call, matching applications are set to
the configured absolute target volume and later restored to their original per-channel values.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/call-ducker/pulse-restore.json
contains crash-safe volume restoration state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR call-duckerctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
